  "limitations": [
    "Scores are provisional browser judgments from the attached screenshots, chronological still filmstrips and supplied runtime summary; I did not run the app or inspect a video.",
    "Corresponding normal, enlarged and transition captures are grouped by task state; viewport variants are grouped where they demonstrate the same behavior.",
    "The authorized A>=9 and F>=9 threshold is not met: several observed hierarchy, typography, surface-integration and focus-feedback deficiencies remain.",
    "No hard-gate failure is established by this evidence; offscreen content in a scrolled or constrained screenshot alone does not prove an unreachable action.",
    "Runtime assertions are supplied evidence rather than independently reproduced measurements; screenshot sampling is not evidence of frame rate.",
    "Native voice, keyboard, sharing, notifications, tilt, haptics, physical iPhone performance and VoiceOver remain unverified without automatic deductions solely for that deferred boundary.",
    "Focus and pressed screenshots do not clearly demonstrate distinct treatments for parchment choices and primary wood buttons, despite stronger demonstrated switch focus.",
    "Filmstrips demonstrate visual changes but do not establish independently painted parallax layers or physically accurate room geometry.",
    "Connected Circles behavior, real billing and actual OS share delivery are outside the demonstrated browser outcomes.",
    "Synthetic layout wording and repeated stress-test prose were assessed for presentation only; neither fixtures nor the supplied live reading establish predictive accuracy.",
    "Repeated novice-use evidence is absent, so exemplary usability outcomes and full/native 9–10 certification are not established."
  ],
